This is a PROTOTYPE, not real content. gen-site.php only loads files
whose name ends in exactly ".entry" — this one ends in ".entry.example",
so it is never loaded, validated, or rendered. It exists purely so a
human (or a content-generation tool) has a blank, all-fields-shown copy
to start from.

To use it:
  1. Copy this file to a new name ending in ".entry", following this
     type's naming convention (see the heading below).
  2. Delete this whole instructional block, including the line of
     dashes, so the file starts with "+++" on the very first line.
  3. Fill in the fields. Leave optional ones blank (or delete the line
     entirely) if they don't apply.
  4. See CONTENT-GUIDE.md for what every field actually does.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Coach landing page — one file per coach (not per domain), named
"<coach_id>.entry", e.g. "jane.entry". Handed out privately (a business
card); never linked to from the site, and must never reveal which
domain(s) this coach actually works in — no domain name anywhere below,
in a field or in the bio.

+++
name:
coach_id:
photo:
photo_side: left
bgimage:
+++

A general bio about this coach's approach, written fresh for this page —
not copied from any domain card, and without naming any domain.
